  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The variation of the acceleration due to gravity with height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Since the weight at given height is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;of the weight at the surface</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>732</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4685</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math></p>"
